WEBVTT

00:00.230 --> 00:03.060
- [Instructor] We are told
Jayden was asked to determine

00:03.060 --> 00:07.720
whether f of x is equal to
x minus the cube root of x

00:07.720 --> 00:10.810
is even, odd, or neither.

00:10.810 --> 00:12.880
Here is his work.

00:12.880 --> 00:15.210
Is Jayden's work correct?

00:15.210 --> 00:19.860
If not, what is the first step
where Jayden made a mistake?

00:19.860 --> 00:22.210
So pause this video and
review Jayden's work,

00:22.210 --> 00:23.580
and see if it's correct,

00:23.580 --> 00:27.380
or if it's not correct tell
me where it's not correct.

00:27.380 --> 00:29.700
All right, now let's work this together.

00:29.700 --> 00:31.470
So, let's see, just to remind ourselves

00:31.470 --> 00:33.670
what Jayden's trying to
do, he's trying to decide,

00:33.670 --> 00:37.760
whether f of x is even, odd, or neither.

00:37.760 --> 00:40.530
And f of x is expressed, or is defined,

00:40.530 --> 00:42.830
as x minus the cube root of x.

00:42.830 --> 00:45.230
So let's see, the first
thing that Jayden did is

00:45.230 --> 00:48.820
he's trying to figure out
what is f of negative x?

00:48.820 --> 00:51.340
Because remember, if f of negative x

00:51.340 --> 00:54.586
is equal to f of x, we are even,

00:54.586 --> 00:56.793
and if f of negative x

00:56.793 --> 01:01.793
is equal to negative f
of x, then we are odd.

01:01.920 --> 01:02.970
So it makes sense for him

01:02.970 --> 01:05.580
to find the expression
for f of negative x.

01:05.580 --> 01:08.630
So he tries to evaluate f of negative x,

01:08.630 --> 01:10.250
and when he does that,

01:10.250 --> 01:12.700
everywhere where he sees an x in f of x,

01:12.700 --> 01:14.760
he replaces it with a negative x.

01:14.760 --> 01:16.510
So that seems good.

01:16.510 --> 01:19.530
And then, let's see, this
becomes a negative x,

01:19.530 --> 01:21.000
that makes sense, minus,

01:21.000 --> 01:24.160
and then, a negative x under the radical,

01:24.160 --> 01:25.780
and this is a cube root right over here,

01:25.780 --> 01:28.710
that's the same thing
as negative one times x.

01:28.710 --> 01:30.660
The cube root of negative
one is negative one.

01:30.660 --> 01:33.390
So he takes that negative
out of the radical,

01:33.390 --> 01:34.560
out of the cube root.

01:34.560 --> 01:38.560
So this makes sense, and
so then he has a negative x

01:38.560 --> 01:41.110
and you subtract a negative,
you get a positive.

01:41.110 --> 01:43.460
So then that makes sense.

01:43.460 --> 01:46.510
And then, the next thing he
says is, or he's trying to do,

01:46.510 --> 01:48.400
is check if f of negative x

01:48.400 --> 01:51.360
is equal to f of x or f of negative x.

01:51.360 --> 01:53.800
So he's gonna check whether
this is equal to one of them.

01:53.800 --> 01:58.440
And so here Jayden says, negative
x plus the cube root of x,

01:58.440 --> 02:02.070
so that's what f of negative
x, what he evaluated it to be,

02:02.070 --> 02:06.750
isn't the same as f of x, now
let's see is that the case?

02:06.750 --> 02:09.644
Is it not the same as f of x?

02:09.644 --> 02:12.691
Yup it's definitely, it's
not the same as f of x,

02:12.691 --> 02:16.640
or negative f of x which is equal to

02:16.640 --> 02:20.288
negative x minus the cube root of x.

02:20.288 --> 02:22.300
Now that seems a little bit fishy.

02:22.300 --> 02:25.920
Did he do the right
thing, right over here?

02:25.920 --> 02:27.640
Is negative f of x equal to

02:27.640 --> 02:29.950
negative x minus the cube root of x?

02:29.950 --> 02:32.770
Let's see, negative of f of x

02:32.770 --> 02:35.380
is going to be a negative
times this entire expression,

02:35.380 --> 02:37.270
it's going to be a negative up front,

02:37.270 --> 02:41.400
times x minus the cube root of x,

02:41.400 --> 02:42.890
and so this is going to be equal to,

02:42.890 --> 02:45.610
you distribute the negative sign,

02:45.610 --> 02:50.290
you get negative x plus
the cube root of x.

02:50.290 --> 02:53.365
So Jayden calculated the wrong

02:53.365 --> 02:56.730
negative f of x right over here.

02:56.730 --> 03:01.730
So, he isn't right that negative
x plus the cube root of x,

03:01.845 --> 03:04.848
it is actually the same
as negative f of x.

03:04.848 --> 03:07.620
So he's wrong right over here.

03:07.620 --> 03:12.200
So Jayden's mistake is right
over here, really it looks like

03:12.200 --> 03:15.460
he didn't evaluate
negative f of x correctly.

03:15.460 --> 03:17.560
So Jayden's work, is
Jayden's work correct?

03:17.560 --> 03:18.540
No.

03:18.540 --> 03:20.970
If not, what is the first step
where Jayden made a mistake?

03:20.970 --> 03:23.130
Well it would be step two.

03:23.130 --> 03:24.686
What he should have said is,

03:24.686 --> 03:28.010
it actually is the same
as negative f of x,

03:28.010 --> 03:30.177
and so therefore his conclusion should be

03:30.177 --> 03:33.273
that f of x is odd.
